/-!
# Quasi-coherent modules on an algebraic stack through a presentation

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack over `S` and let `[U/R] → 𝒳` be a presentation of `𝒳`: a smooth
groupoid `(U, R, s, t, c)` in algebraic spaces over `S` together with an equivalence
`[U/R] → 𝒳` (Stacks 04TI).  Then
$$\mathrm{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal{X}) \cong \mathrm{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{[U/R]}) \cong
\mathrm{QCoh}(U, R, s, t, c),$$
the first equivalence being the inverse image along the equivalence `[U/R] → 𝒳` and the second
Stacks 06WT.  Every algebraic stack has a presentation (Stacks 04T3), and the quasi-coherent
modules on a groupoid whose source and target are flat form an abelian category (Stacks 06VZ), so
`QCoh(𝒪_𝒳)` is abelian.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.GroupoidPresentation.quasicoherentEquivalence`: **Stacks 06WV (1)**,
  the equivalence `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) ≌ QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` attached to a presentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.abelianQuasicoherentModules`: **Stacks 06WV (2)**, the abelian
  structure on `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.GroupoidPresentation.exists_ofArrows_basedFunctor`: every object of
  `𝒳` is covered by the image of an object of `[U/R]`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.abelianQuasicoherentModules_toPreadditive`: the abelian structure has
  the preadditive structure of the full subcategory `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) ⊆ Mod(𝒪_𝒳)`.

Parts (5) and (6) of Stacks 06WV, that `𝓕 ⊗ 𝓖` is quasi-coherent and that `ℋom(𝓕, 𝓖)` is
quasi-coherent for `𝓕` finite locally free, are
`AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.isQuasicoherentOnSite_sheafTensor` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.internalHomSheaf_isQuasicoherent`, which hold for every category
fibred in groupoids over `(Sch/S)_fppf`; they are registered against the tag below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06WV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06WV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06WT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06WT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06VZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06VZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04T3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04T3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04TI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04TI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe w u

add_to_stacks 06WV "part (5): for quasi-coherent F, G the tensor product F ⊗ G computed in \
  Mod(𝒪_𝒳) is quasi-coherent, for every category fibred in groupoids over (Sch/S)_fppf (at \
  τ = fppf)" AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.isQuasicoherentOnSite_sheafTensor

add_to_stacks 06WV "part (6): for F, G in QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) with F finite locally free, the internal \
  Hom ℋom(F, G) computed in Mod(𝒪_𝒳) is quasi-coherent, for every category fibred in groupoids \
  over (Sch/S)_fppf" AlgebraicGeometry.FibredSite.internalHomSheaf_isQuasicoherent

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- **Every object of `𝒳` is covered by the image of an object of `[U/R]`**, for a presentation
`[U/R] → 𝒳`: the presenting 1-morphism is essentially surjective, so each object of `𝒳` is
isomorphic to an image, and the sieve generated by an isomorphism is the maximal one. -/
theorem GroupoidPresentation.exists_ofArrows_basedFunctor {𝒳 : AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS}
    (P : GroupoidPresentation B S hS 𝒳.val.val) (y : 𝒳.val.val.obj) :
    ∃ (I : Type u) (x : I → (quotientStack P.groupoid).obj)
      (g : ∀ i, P.basedFunctor.toFunctor.obj (x i) ⟶ y),
      Sieve.ofArrows _ g ∈ associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p B.topology y := by
  refine ⟨PUnit, fun _ => P.basedFunctor.toFunctor.objPreimage y,
    fun _ => (P.basedFunctor.toFunctor.objObjPreimageIso y).hom, ?_⟩
  refine GrothendieckTopology.superset_covering _ ?_ (GrothendieckTopology.top_mem _ y)
  intro Z h _
  rw [Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff]
  exact ⟨PUnit.unit, h ≫ (P.basedFunctor.toFunctor.objObjPreimageIso y).inv, by simp⟩

/-- **Stacks 06WV (1).**  A presentation `[U/R] → 𝒳` of an algebraic stack — a smooth groupoid
`(U, R, s, t, c)` in algebraic spaces over `S` and an equivalence `[U/R] → 𝒳` (Stacks 04TI) —
induces a canonical equivalence `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) ≌ QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)`.

It is the inverse image along the presenting equivalence, `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) ≌ QCoh(𝒪_{[U/R]})`,
followed by the equivalence of Stacks 06WT,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.quasicoherentEquivalenceGroupoid`. -/
@[stacks 06WV "part (1): a presentation [U/R] → 𝒳 induces a canonical equivalence \
  QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) ≌ QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)"]
def GroupoidPresentation.quasicoherentEquivalence {𝒳 : AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS}
    (P : GroupoidPresentation B S hS 𝒳.val.val) :
    FibredSite.quasicoherentModules.{u, u + 1, u, u} B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p
        𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids ≌ Space.QuasicoherentModule B S hS P.groupoid :=
  haveI := isEquivalence_quasicoherentPullback'_of_full_of_faithful.{u, u + 1, u + 1, u, u + 1, u}
    B S hS _ _ (isFiberedInGroupoids_quotientStack P.groupoid) 𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids
    P.basedFunctor.toFunctor P.basedFunctor.w P.exists_ofArrows_basedFunctor
  (quasicoherentPullback'.{u, u + 1, u + 1, u, u + 1, u} B S hS _ _
    (isFiberedInGroupoids_quotientStack P.groupoid) 𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids
    P.basedFunctor.toFunctor P.basedFunctor.w).asEquivalence.trans
    (quasicoherentEquivalenceGroupoid P.groupoid)

/-- **Stacks 06WV (2).**  The quasi-coherent modules on an algebraic stack form an abelian
category.

By Stacks 04T3 the stack has a presentation `[U/R] → 𝒳` by a smooth groupoid; its source and
target are smooth, hence flat, so `QCoh(U, R, s, t, c)` is abelian by Stacks 06VZ, and part (1)
transports the abelian structure to `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳)`. -/
@[stacks 06WV "part (2): QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) is abelian"]
instance abelianQuasicoherentModules (𝒳 : AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS) :
    Abelian (FibredSite.quasicoherentModules.{u, u + 1, u, u} B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p
      𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids) :=
  let P := (nonempty_groupoidPresentation B S hS 𝒳.val 𝒳.property).some
  letI := Space.QuasicoherentModule.abelian_of_closure P.groupoid
    (Space.isFlat_of_isSmooth B S hS _ P.smooth.1) (Space.isFlat_of_isSmooth B S hS _ P.smooth.2)
  FibredSite.abelianQuasicoherentModulesOfEquivalence B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p
    𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids P.quasicoherentEquivalence.functor

/-- The abelian structure of Stacks 06WV (2) has the preadditive structure of the full
subcategory `QCoh(𝒪_𝒳) ⊆ Mod(𝒪_𝒳)`. -/
theorem abelianQuasicoherentModules_toPreadditive (𝒳 : AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS) :
    (abelianQuasicoherentModules 𝒳).toPreadditive =
      (inferInstance : Preadditive (FibredSite.quasicoherentModules.{u, u + 1, u, u} B S hS
        𝒳.val.val.p 𝒳.val.isFiberedInGroupoids)) := rfl

end AlgebraicGeometry.Stack

end
